{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cfe77f003e65e3c77e855a8ea37afcab888b6eead4c9d253cf7714d666947aa1","digest":{"component_or_area":"scripts/gen_env_registry.py","key_entities":["scripts/gen_env_registry.py","docs/env-vars.md","os.environ.get","os.environ.pop","os.environ.setdefault","os.environ.__getitem__","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","scripts/check_config_ownership.py","tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","UnrecognisedEnvironAccess","KEY_BEARING","KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS"],"problem_keywords":["environment variable registry","documentation drift","AST scanning","silent omission","generator blindness"],"propositions":["The generator recognises only os.environ.get, os.environ[...] subscript, and os.getenv forms; it silently skips unrecognised attribute access like os.environ.pop, causing environment variables read via those methods to disappear from docs/env-vars.md without error.","Refactoring os.environ.get to os.environ.pop silently drops the variable from generated documentation; the CI drift gate passes because the stale doc agrees with the blind generator output.","An unrecognised os.environ attribute access must raise an UnrecognisedEnvironAccess error rather than silently skip, so novel read forms fail the build instead of quietly omitting keys.","The local make lint gate must run the generator's --check to match CI verdicts and catch documentation drift before submission."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787439031328228760,"uuid":"c22eac71-6ca4-4628-86cf-72cef104f9a7"}